4. Debate protocol & state machine (docs/protocol.md)

WebSocket message schema (JSON)

- Common fields:
  - type: message type string.
  - payload: type‑specific data.

Node → Arena

- JOIN
  - payload: { "name": str, "persona": str, "version": str }
- TOKENS
  - payload: { "speaker": str, "chunk": str, "final": bool }
- HEARTBEAT
  - payload: { "name": str }
- ERROR
  - payload: { "name": str, "message": str }

Arena → Node

- WELCOME
  - payload: { "chairkeyrequired": bool }
- SPEAK
  - payload: { "prompt": str, "context": [turns], "ent_mode": bool }
- STOP
  - payload: { "reason": "interrupt" | "timeout" }
- PING
  - payload: {}

Debate state machine

States:

- IDLE
- READY (nodes joined, chair present)
- RUNNING
- PAUSED
- FINISHED

Transitions:

- IDLE → READY when ≥2 nodes joined.
- READY → RUNNING on START_DEBATE.
- RUNNING → PAUSED on PAUSE.
- PAUSED → RUNNING on RESUME.
- RUNNING → FINISHED on END_DEBATE.

Turn logic (hybrid style):

- Chair‑driven:  
  - Chair presses “Next speaker” → Arena selects next from roster (round‑robin or weighted).
- Optional auto‑advance:  
  - Timer‑based; when node finishes or timeout, auto‑advance.

